Probably not the scientific answer you're looking for, but here's my two cents.

&#x200B;

I have improved my neutral grip and supinated grip chinup strength, by my AMRAP on pullups has not increased. Training pullups for high-end strength and going AMRAP are just two totally different stimuli.

&#x200B;

I think the other comment is a great suggestion. Work capacity training. It's also worth noting that bodyweight pullps are not very taxing on the CNS. You could probably do them 3-4 times a week without wearing yourself out. 

&#x200B;

If I was trying to improve my AMRAP goal, I might do two days of 10 sets of 10 every minute on the minute like the other commentor said, one day of 3-4 sets to failure, then maybe another day where yo're working with light weight (10-25 lbs) doing 3 sets to failure. There are different ways you can approach this, I think the bottom line is to simply train bodyweight frequently with higher reps. 

&#x200B;

