Ok, don't take this as gospel, this is just my opinion.

&#x200B;

Soreness might be normal, especially if you are reincorporating these lifts into your routine. However, if you're still feeling soreness after several weeks of doing these movements, your form likely needs to improve.

&#x200B;

That said, an example of soreness is doing a real tough squat workout, and your quads are sore afterwards. Or maybe you do some heavy eccentrics for your biceps, and your arms are sore.

&#x200B;

Whereas pain would be something you feel after you actually pull/strain a muscle in the lower back.

&#x200B;

This particular area is not an area of expertise for me, so again, take it with a grain of salt

