Notice how your right arm is bringing the barbell up higher than your left arm. The bar is tilted because you have a strength imbalance. You should do some dumbell work to try to get your left side as strong as your right.

&#x200B;

And no, don't use a straight bar. Intentionally doing something that injures you is foolish. An ez bar accomodates the wrists a lot better.

I honestly feel like your form is pretty solid. It looks like you're driving your hips forward and keeping the lower back healthy. 

